 of  spare capacity to operate the  electricity system securely over this  evening's peak demand period  the government has announced the winners  of a 23 million pound competition to  help international shipping reach net  zero by  but shipping leaders called the funding  a drop in the ocean in an open letter to  the chancellor and say that the  government must co-invest one billion  pounds to decarbonize the sector  transport secretary grant shaps had this  to say about the letter  although a billion pounds is a huge  amount of money when you take that  in the round of what it costs to build  ships  and the sector as a whole that kind of  money flows in uh pretty regularly from  the private sector now the government  and i can't preempt what the chancellor  will say at the spending review but the  government will do its part in leading  this industry we want absolute zero by  2050 in maritime so that's not just  about money it's about making sure that  we get the right diplomatic backdrop to  all of this as well  now the 2019 to 2020 australian  wildfires released more than twice as  much carbon dioxide into the atmosphere  than previously thought that's according  to a study published in nature and a  separate paper has found that the smoke  from those fires traveled thousands of  miles before settling on the water  triggering a phytoplankton bloom bigger  than australia itself scientists say  that the findings highlight the complex  links between wildfires and ecosystems  and today is the 50th anniversary of  greenpeace beginning environmental  campaigning the movement started when a  ship carrying a group of activists left  canada for a small island off the coast  of alaska in an attempt to stop the u.s  government testing nuclear devices or  greenpeace say that its goals in 2021  include stopping new fossil fuel  projects and making green recovery fair  for everyone  now more than 70 people have been  arrested after climate protesters  blocked parts of the m25